{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Experiment 01 — HUGS Locality Probe\n",
    "\n",
    "Google Colab setup for the first **Interactive Digital Humans / 4D Human Intelligence** diagnostic experiment.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook reproduces a HUGS pretrained human and measures how much a local SMPL joint perturbation changes Gaussian regions outside the intended target.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 0. Runtime\n", "Choose **A100 GPU** when available.\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!nvidia-smi\n",
    "import torch, platform\n",
    "print('Colab Python:', platform.python_version())\n",
    "print('Colab PyTorch:', torch.__version__)\n",
    "print('CUDA available:', torch.cuda.is_available())\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available(): print('GPU:', torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 1. Clone repositories\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%cd /content\n",
    "!rm -rf interactive-digital-humans ml-hugs\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/reusahn/interactive-digital-humans.git\n",
    "!git clone --recursive https://github.com/apple-aiml-research/ml-hugs.git\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Create pinned HUGS environment\n",
    "\n",
    "HUGS was released against Python 3.8, PyTorch 1.13.1 and CUDA 11.7. We isolate those versions from Colab's current Python/CUDA stack.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, subprocess\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_live(cmd, cwd=None, env=None):\n",
    "    print('\\n+', cmd, flush=True)\n",
    "    p = subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True, cwd=cwd, env=env, text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)\n",
    "    print(p.stdout)\n",
    "    if p.returncode != 0:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(f'Command failed with exit code {p.returncode}: {cmd}')\n",
    "    return p\n",
    "\n",
    "run_live('wget -q https://github.com/conda-forge/miniforge/releases/latest/download/Miniforge3-Linux-x86_64.sh -O /content/miniforge.sh')\n",
    "run_live('bash /content/miniforge.sh -b -p /content/miniforge')\n",
    "run_live('/content/miniforge/bin/conda env remove -n hugs -y || true')\n",
    "run_live('/content/miniforge/bin/conda create -n hugs python=3.8 pip -y -c conda-forge')\n",
    "run_live('/content/miniforge/bin/conda install -n hugs -y -c nvidia/label/cuda-11.7.0 cuda-toolkit=11.7.0')\n",
    "# CUDA 11.7 does not support the newest host GCC used by current Colab images.\n",
    "run_live('/content/miniforge/bin/conda install -n hugs -y -c conda-forge gcc_linux-64=11 gxx_linux-64=11')\n",
    "\n",
    "PY = '/content/miniforge/envs/hugs/bin/python'\n",
    "PIP = f'{PY} -m pip'\n",
    "run_live(f\"{PIP} install --upgrade 'pip<25' 'setuptools<70' wheel ninja\")\n",
    "run_live(f'{PIP} install torch==1.13.1+cu117 torchvision==0.14.1+cu117 torchaudio==0.13.1 --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu117')\n",
    "run_live(f'{PIP} install numpy==1.23.5 fvcore iopath')\n",
    "run_live(f'{PIP} install --no-index --no-cache-dir pytorch3d -f https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/pytorch3d/packaging/wheels/py38_cu117_pyt1131/download.html')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2B. Build HUGS CUDA extensions\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell is intentionally separate. If an extension fails, it prints the **full compiler log** instead of hiding it behind `CalledProcessError`.\n",
    "\n",
    "If your previous run already created the `hugs` environment, you can start here after first running the small repair cell below.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, subprocess, pathlib\n",
    "\n",
    "CONDA = '/content/miniforge/bin/conda'\n",
    "PREFIX = '/content/miniforge/envs/hugs'\n",
    "PY = f'{PREFIX}/bin/python'\n",
    "PIP = f'{PY} -m pip'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Safe to run even if GCC 11 is already installed.\n",
    "run_live(f'{CONDA} install -n hugs -y -c conda-forge gcc_linux-64=11 gxx_linux-64=11')\n",
    "\n",
    "build_env = os.environ.copy()\n",
    "build_env['CUDA_HOME'] = PREFIX\n",
    "build_env['PATH'] = f\"{PREFIX}/bin:\" + build_env.get('PATH', '')\n",
    "build_env['LD_LIBRARY_PATH'] = f\"{PREFIX}/lib:{PREFIX}/lib64:\" + build_env.get('LD_LIBRARY_PATH', '')\n",
    "build_env['CC'] = f'{PREFIX}/bin/x86_64-conda-linux-gnu-cc'\n",
    "build_env['CXX'] = f'{PREFIX}/bin/x86_64-conda-linux-gnu-c++'\n",
    "build_env['CUDAHOSTCXX'] = build_env['CXX']\n",
    "build_env['TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST'] = '8.0'\n",
    "build_env['MAX_JOBS'] = '2'\n",
    "build_env['FORCE_CUDA'] = '1'\n",
    "\n",
    "print('CUDA_HOME =', build_env['CUDA_HOME'])\n",
    "run_live(f'{PREFIX}/bin/nvcc --version', env=build_env)\n",
    "run_live(f'{build_env[\"CC\"]} --version', env=build_env)\n",
    "run_live(f'{PY} -c \\"import torch; print(torch.__version__, torch.version.cuda, torch.cuda.is_available()); print(torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\\"', env=build_env)\n",
    "\n",
    "# --no-build-isolation ensures the extension sees the pinned torch installation.\n",
    "run_live(f'{PIP} install -v --no-build-isolation ./submodules/diff-gaussian-rasterization', cwd='/content/ml-hugs', env=build_env)\n",
    "run_live(f'{PIP} install -v --no-build-isolation ./submodules/simple-knn', cwd='/content/ml-hugs', env=build_env)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 2C. Install remaining Python dependencies and verify imports\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "run_live(f'{PIP} install -r requirements.txt', cwd='/content/ml-hugs', env=build_env)\n",
    "run_live(f'{PIP} install git+https://github.com/mattloper/chumpy.git', cwd='/content/ml-hugs', env=build_env)\n",
    "run_live(f'{PY} -c \\"import torch, diff_gaussian_rasterization, simple_knn; print(\\\"torch\\\", torch.__version__); print(\\\"CUDA\\\", torch.version.cuda); print(\\\"GPU\\\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)); print(\\\"CUDA extensions: OK\\\")\\"', cwd='/content/ml-hugs', env=build_env)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 3. Download NeuMan data and pretrained HUGS models\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%cd /content/ml-hugs\n",
    "!bash scripts/prepare_data_models.sh\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Upload licensed SMPL neutral model\n",
    "\n",
    "Download SMPL v1.1.0 from the official SMPL site. Upload the neutral `.pkl`; this notebook renames it to `SMPL_NEUTRAL.pkl`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import shutil\n",
    "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
    "smpl_dir = Path('/content/ml-hugs/data/smpl')\n",
    "smpl_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "for name in uploaded:\n",
    "    src = Path(name)\n",
    "    if name.endswith('.pkl'):\n",
    "        dst = smpl_dir / 'SMPL_NEUTRAL.pkl'\n",
    "    elif name == 'smpl_uv.obj':\n",
    "        dst = smpl_dir / 'smpl_uv.obj'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        continue\n",
    "    shutil.move(str(src), str(dst))\n",
    "    print('Saved:', dst)\n",
    "assert (smpl_dir / 'SMPL_NEUTRAL.pkl').exists()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 5. Find a pretrained output directory\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "root = Path('/content/ml-hugs')\n",
    "configs = list(root.rglob('config_train.yaml'))\n",
    "for i, p in enumerate(configs): print(i, p.parent)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "HUGS_OUTPUT_DIR = ''  # paste a human or human_scene pretrained directory above\n",
    "p = Path(HUGS_OUTPUT_DIR)\n",
    "assert HUGS_OUTPUT_DIR and (p / 'config_train.yaml').exists()\n",
    "print('Using:', p)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 6. Official HUGS evaluation sanity check\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "run_live(f'{PY} scripts/evaluate.py -o \\"{HUGS_OUTPUT_DIR}\\"', cwd='/content/ml-hugs', env=build_env)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 7. Run locality probe: left wrist +10°\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cmd = f'''{PY} hugs_locality_probe.py --hugs-root /content/ml-hugs --output-dir \"{HUGS_OUTPUT_DIR}\" --frame 0 --joint left_wrist --axis z --degrees 10 --save-dir /content/probe_results'''\n",
    "run_live(cmd, cwd='/content/interactive-digital-humans/experiments/01-baseline', env=build_env)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json, glob\n",
    "files = sorted(glob.glob('/content/probe_results/frame*.json'))\n",
    "assert files\n",
    "with open(files[-1]) as f: result = json.load(f)\n",
    "result\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": ["## 8. Save results to Google Drive\n"]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import shutil, datetime\n",
    "stamp = datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y%m%d_%H%M%S')\n",
    "dst = Path('/content/drive/MyDrive/interactive-digital-humans/experiment-01') / stamp\n",
    "dst.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "shutil.copytree('/content/probe_results', dst)\n",
    "print('Saved to:', dst)\n"
   ]
  }
